        "id": "us-doj-directory-summary",
        "page": null,
        "section": "Find support in your area",
        "text": "For local domestic violence support, the U.S. Department of Justice lists national hotlines and state, territory, and Tribal coalitions. These organizations can connect survivors with direct service providers. The Office on Violence Against Women itself does not provide direct services or assist with individual cases.",
